screen.DISTANT_HAZE_SETTINGS=Distant Haze
screen.DISTANT_HAZE_SETTINGS.comment=Aerial perspective: the air between you and far terrain and clouds tints them blue, then fades them into the horizon. §e[*]§r Works with and without Distant Horizons or Voxy, at fixed distances set here.
option.DISTANT_HAZE=霾强度
option.DISTANT_HAZE.comment=How thick the air is. §e[*]§r 100 is a clear day; raise it for hazier, more distant-looking landscapes. §e[*]§r 0 turns the haze off.
value.DISTANT_HAZE.0=关
option.HAZE_BLUE=雾霭蓝度
option.HAZE_BLUE.comment=Colour of the distant haze. §e[*]§r 0 is the colour of the horizon, which is almost white when the sun is low. §e[*]§r Higher values take the blue of the sky above it, so far mountains turn the blue they are in reality.
option.HAZE_START=Haze Start
option.HAZE_START.comment=Distance where the haze begins. Nearer than this the air stays clear.
suffix.HAZE_START=方块
option.HAZE_DISTANCE=Full Haze Distance
option.HAZE_DISTANCE.comment=Distance at which the haze fully hides the terrain. Higher values show more of the far terrain. Keep it well beyond your Distant Horizons or Voxy distance, or the farthest LOD disappears into the haze. §e[*]§r Fixed: it does not follow the render distance or the distance set in Distant Horizons or Voxy.
suffix.HAZE_DISTANCE=方块
option.CLOUD_HAZE=Clouds in Distant Haze
option.CLOUD_HAZE.comment=Far clouds pale and turn bluish in the distant haze, and dissolve into the sky only in the last few degrees above the horizon, as they do in real air. Clouds higher in the sky stay clear. Works with every cloud style. §e[*]§r Needs Haze Strength above 0 in Atmosphere > Distant Haze.
value.CLOUD_HAZE.0=关
value.CLOUD_HAZE.1=开
screen.CUSTOM_SKYBOX_SETTINGS=Custom Skybox
screen.CUSTOM_SKYBOX_SETTINGS.comment=Show a resource pack custom sky properly. Needs a pack that ships one -- optifine/sky/world0/sky1.png and its .properties -- and an Iris build that loads them.
option.CUSTOM_SKYBOX=Custom Skybox
option.CUSTOM_SKYBOX.comment=How a resource pack sky texture is drawn. §e[*]§r §bOff§r is the old behaviour: the texture is faded out towards the horizon and is only really visible overhead. §e[*]§r §bBlend§r keeps a gentle falloff so it still sits inside the pack sky. §e[*]§r §eFull§r draws it as authored, all the way down. §e[*]§r Clouds, aurora, nebula and fog are drawn afterwards and still sit on top of it.
value.CUSTOM_SKYBOX.0=关
value.CUSTOM_SKYBOX.1=§bBlend
value.CUSTOM_SKYBOX.2=§4§l§n§o完整
option.CUSTOM_SKYBOX_I=天空盒亮度
option.CUSTOM_SKYBOX_I.comment=Brightness of the sky texture. §e[*]§r 100 matches how bright it was straight overhead before. Raise it if your skybox looks dim against the rest of the scene -- it is converted from sRGB the same way the sun is, which darkens it on purpose.
option.CUSTOM_SKYBOX_RAIN=Keep In Rain
option.CUSTOM_SKYBOX_RAIN.comment=How much of the skybox survives rain. §e[*]§r At 0 it disappears in a downpour the way the sun does; at 100 the weather does not touch it. Sun and moon keep their own behaviour either way.
option.SUN_MOON_DURING_RAIN=雨天太阳/月亮
option.SUN_MOON_DURING_RAIN.comment=决定雨天是否显示太阳和月亮。
option.ALWAYS_REALISTIC_MOON=Always Realistic Moon (Unb.)
option.ALWAYS_REALISTIC_MOON.comment=Shows the HD photo of the moon at all times, not only while zoomed in with Space Zoom Moon. The moon keeps the phases and fading of its style. Near the horizon it grows, turns yellow, then orange, and sinks into the haze with a soft glow, as the real moon does when it rises. §e[*]§r Works only with Sun/Moon Style §dUnbound§r or §dUnbound - Smaller§r. With §bReimagined§r it has no effect.
value.ALWAYS_REALISTIC_MOON.0=关
value.ALWAYS_REALISTIC_MOON.1=开

