screen.DEBUG_SETTINGS=调试
screen.DEBUG_SETTINGS.comment=资源包中所有诊断视图的集合。[*] 每个视图都会用渲染管线中的某个阶段替换最终画面，这样故障可以定位到产生它的阶段而非显示它的阶段。[-] 所有视图默认关闭，启用时不会产生额外性能消耗。[*] 注意用完后要关闭——其中几个视图乍看之下很像正常画面，容易被误判为渲染错误。 

option.VX_DEBUG=光线追踪视图
option.VX_DEBUG.comment=Shows the voxel tracer itself rather than the light it produces. §e[*]§r §oVoxel Colour§r is what a bounce reflects off -- a surface stored in the wrong colour throws wrong-coloured light no matter how good the trace is. §e[*]§r §oDistance Field§r is how far the tracer believes it can step without hitting anything, drawn as contours; a fault in the field shows as a kink in a contour long before it shows as a shade. §e[*]§r §oCascade Level§r is which resolution of that field is being read, and comes out as boxes nested around you -- an artefact that follows you is usually born on one of those seams. §e[*]§r §oSky Exposure§r is the per-voxel sky value the bounce is traced against, black none to white full. §e[*]§r §oBounce Hit§r fires one ray along the surface normal and paints what it landed on, so you can see where the light on a surface is coming from; dark blue means it escaped to open sky. §e[*]§r §oBounce Distance§r is how far that ray got, blue near to red at the limit, black if it escaped. §e[*]§r §oTrace Cost§r is what that ray cost against its step budget, green cheap to red spent -- this is the one to read about frame time, and every red pixel is paying that cost once per GI sample, not once per frame. §e[*]§r The probe is fired along the normal rather than in a random direction so the picture holds still while you look at it.
value.VX_DEBUG.0=关
value.VX_DEBUG.1=体素颜色
value.VX_DEBUG.2=距离场
value.VX_DEBUG.3=级联层级
value.VX_DEBUG.4=天空曝光
value.VX_DEBUG.5=弹射命中
value.VX_DEBUG.6=弹射距离
value.VX_DEBUG.7=追踪耗时

option.SELECT_OUTLINE_BETTER=§eBetter SO
option.SELECT_OUTLINE_BETTER.comment=Traces the selected block's own texture instead of only boxing it. The rim is drawn on the EMPTY side of the boundary, just outside the shape, so it reads as an outline rather than filling the shape in. §e[*]§r Glow lichen, vines, a ladder, a rail: all of them are a cutout painted on a full-size quad, so the ordinary outline draws a rectangle around a shape that fills almost none of it. This follows the shape itself -- its silhouette and the holes inside it -- and leaves the box where it is. §e[*]§r Solid blocks are untouched and need no list: the trace only fires where the texture actually turns transparent, and samples are clamped to the sprite so a stone block can never see the transparent one packed next to it in the atlas. §e[*]§r Uses the outline colour from this page in every mode except Rainbow, where it matches the animated box. In §oDefault§r the box is vanilla black, so the traced line uses the colour chosen here to stay visible. §c[-]§r Iris only -- it needs the selected-block position, which OptiFine does not provide. §e[*]§r Default: §aOFF§r.
value.SELECT_OUTLINE_BETTER.0=关
value.SELECT_OUTLINE_BETTER.1=开

option.SELECT_OUTLINE_BETTER_WIDTH=优化轮廓线宽度
option.SELECT_OUTLINE_BETTER_WIDTH.comment=追踪轮廓线的粗细，单位为屏幕像素。[*] 刻意以屏幕像素而非纹理纹素为单位：纹理像素宽度的线条在远处呈现为发丝细线，近处则变为粗条，而此功能可使轮廓线在任意距离下都保持与所在方框一致的视觉权重。[*] 默认：0.00。 

option.SELECT_OUTLINE_BETTER_IGNORE_LEAVES=优化轮廓——忽略树叶
option.SELECT_OUTLINE_BETTER_IGNORE_LEAVES.comment=Leaves out leaf blocks. §e[*]§r A leaf block is holes all the way through, so tracing one draws a rim around every gap in the canopy at once and reads as noise rather than as an outline. §e[*]§r Off, leaves are traced like anything else. §e[*]§r Default: §aON§r.
value.SELECT_OUTLINE_BETTER_IGNORE_LEAVES.0=关
value.SELECT_OUTLINE_BETTER_IGNORE_LEAVES.1=开

option.CLOUD_OUTLINE=云层轮廓
option.CLOUD_OUTLINE.comment=Draws an outline along the silhouette of the clouds, so they are edged like the world below them instead of being the one soft thing in the frame. §e[*]§r Costs nothing measurable: the edge comes from the screen-space rate of change of the clouds' own coverage, which is one instruction and no extra sampling. §e[*]§r Independent of World Outline -- either can be on without the other. §e[*]§r Default: §aOFF§r.
value.CLOUD_OUTLINE.0=关
value.CLOUD_OUTLINE.1=开
value.WORLD_OUTLINE.0=关
value.WORLD_OUTLINE.1=开
value.DARK_OUTLINE.0=关
value.DARK_OUTLINE.1=开


screen.PP_CINEMA_SETTINGS=电影级
screen.PP_CINEMA_SETTINGS.comment=画幅要呈现胶片质感必须处理的两个元素，是其余资源包无法控制的：画幅形状与胶片颗粒。[*] 影视感的其他要素均已存在——色调映射、色温、泛光、动态模糊、景深等——因此本页面不重复实现这些功能。[*] 两者都在最后阶段处理，即在所有替换画幅而非叠加效果的处理完成后运行。 

option.CINEMA_LETTERBOX=信箱模式
option.CINEMA_LETTERBOX.comment=Matte bars top and bottom, sized to crop the window to a chosen aspect. §e[*]§r Sized from the real aspect of your window rather than as a fixed fraction of its height, so the frame inside them is the ratio you asked for on any display. §e[*]§r A window already wider than the target gets no bars at all. §e[*]§r Default: §aOFF§r.
value.CINEMA_LETTERBOX.0=关
value.CINEMA_LETTERBOX.1=开

option.CINEMA_LETTERBOX_RATIO=宽高比
option.CINEMA_LETTERBOX_RATIO.comment=遮幅裁剪的目标比例值（乘以100）。[*] 对应变形宽银幕比例（常见最宽格式，现代电影常用），对应标准影院比例，而几乎不裁剪16:9窗口。[*] 默认值：。 

option.CINEMA_GRAIN=胶片颗粒
option.CINEMA_GRAIN.comment=Grain weighted the way film grains, strongest in the midtones and falling away at both ends. §e[*]§r That is not a stylistic choice: grain is the statistics of how many crystals happened to develop, so where almost none or almost all of them did -- deep shadow and blown highlight -- there is nothing left to vary. Applying it flat is what makes digital grain look like noise sitting on the picture instead of being part of it. §e[*]§r Achromatic for the same reason: scanned colour negative grain is dominated by luminance, and per-channel noise reads as chroma error. §e[*]§r Default: §aOFF§r.
value.CINEMA_GRAIN.0=关
value.CINEMA_GRAIN.1=开

option.CINEMA_GRAIN_I=噪点强度
option.CINEMA_GRAIN_I.comment=颗粒强度振幅（千分比）。[*] 建议保持低值——在肉眼难以察觉的强度下呈现纹理感，强度过高则易在达到胶片感前显现为噪点。[*] 默认值：。 

option.CINEMA_GRAIN_SIZE=颗粒大小
option.CINEMA_GRAIN_SIZE.comment=单颗粒尺寸（屏幕像素）。[*] 数值1为最精细且高分辨率下最真实的呈现；较大数值模拟更高速/粗糙的胶片感，且更能抵抗视频压缩。[*] 默认值：。 


screen.PP_FILTER_SETTINGS=过滤器
screen.PP_FILTER_SETTINGS.comment=应用于成品画幅的摄影滤镜。[*] 刻意混合两类处理：一是真实胶片/化学处理/镜头玻璃产生的物理效果；二是单纯视觉效果良好的常规调色。[*] 仅编译所选滤镜，列表长度不影响性能。 

option.PP_FILTERS=过滤器
option.PP_FILTERS.comment=Applies a photographic filter to the finished frame. §c[-]§r The §f§lCinematic§r post profile forces this ON with City Night at full strength, and a post profile cannot show that here -- this page keeps displaying your own stored choice while the shader compiles with the preset's. §e[*]§r Runs before the film grain and the letterbox: a filter is glass in front of the lens, not something sprinkled on the print. §e[*]§r Default: §aOFF§r.
value.PP_FILTERS.0=关
value.PP_FILTERS.1=开

